{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ships as a separate library target alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It provides a single domain plugin (","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), a state slice, an action enum, and a pluggable challenge generator. For task-oriented integration, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". For the underlying plugin contract, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Library target","type":"heading","anchor":"Library-target"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" product as a target dependency, then import it where you wire the store and present the gate sheet:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiduxParentalGate"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The package vends three library products: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":". Pull in only what you use."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Types","type":"heading","anchor":"Types"},{"level":3,"text":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"heading","anchor":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":"-bound domain plugin generic over the host app’s root state and action types."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@MainActor","public struct ParentalGatePlugin<RootState, RootAction>: SwiduxPlugin {","    public typealias State = RootState","    public typealias Action = RootAction","","    public init(","        state: WritableKeyPath<RootState, ParentalGateState>,","        action toRootAction: @escaping @Sendable (ParentalGateAction) -> RootAction,","        extractAction: @escaping @Sendable (RootAction) -> ParentalGateAction?,","        challengeSource: ParentalChallengeSource = .standard","    )","","    public func reduce(state: inout RootState, action: RootAction) -> Effect<RootAction>?","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The three wiring closures follow the standard domain-plugin shape described in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a keypath into the host’s state, a lifter from local to root action, and an extractor from root to local action."}]},{"level":3,"text":"ParentalGateState","type":"heading","anchor":"ParentalGateState"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The state slice the plugin owns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public struct ParentalGateState: Sendable, Equatable {","    public var pendingReason: String?","    public var challenge: MathChallenge?","    public var attempts: Int","    public var passedReasons: Set<String>","","    public init(","        pendingReason: String? = nil,","        challenge: MathChallenge? = nil,","        attempts: Int = 0,","        passedReasons: Set<String> = []","    )","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pendingReason"},{"type":"text","text":" — non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" while a challenge is active. Drives sheet presentation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the currently-presented arithmetic problem."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — count of incorrect submissions against the current challenge."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — reasons already cleared this session (see action semantics below)."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"ParentalGateAction","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"ParentalGateAction"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public enum ParentalGateAction: Sendable {","    case request(reason: String)","    case dismiss","    case regenerateChallenge","    case submitAnswer(Int)","    case answerAccepted(reason: String)","    case answerRejected","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"MathChallenge","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"MathChallenge"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["public struct MathChallenge: Sendable, Equatable {","    public let left: Int","    public let right: Int","    public let op: Op","","    public init(left: Int, right: Int, op: Op)","","    public var expected: Int","","    public enum Op: String, Sendable, CaseIterable {","        case plus, minus, times","","        public var symbol: String  \/\/ \"+\", \"−\", \"×\"","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expected"},{"type":"text","text":" computes the correct answer from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"left"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"right"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"op"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Op.symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" returns a display-friendly Unicode glyph (minus sign U+2212, multiplication sign U+00D7)."}]},{"anchor":"ParentalChallengeSource","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A value-type holder for a challenge generator closure."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ParentalChallengeSource: Sendable {","    public var generate: @Sendable () -> MathChallenge","","    public init(generate: @escaping @Sendable () -> MathChallenge)","","    public static let standard: ParentalChallengeSource","    public static func fixed(_ challenge: MathChallenge) -> ParentalChallengeSource","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource.standard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — random, age-appropriate challenges. Plus and minus use operands in the 10–40 range; times uses 3–9. Subtraction is always non-negative.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource.fixed(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — always returns the supplied challenge. Use this in tests.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Action-semantics","type":"heading","text":"Action semantics","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGateAction"},{"type":"text","text":" case mutates the state slice as follows:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request(reason:)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":" already contains "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reason"},{"text":", the plugin returns an effect that immediately dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".answerAccepted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and leaves "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pendingReason"},{"type":"text","text":" unchanged. Otherwise, it sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pendingReason"},{"type":"text","text":", generates a fresh "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge"},{"type":"text","text":", and resets "},{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":".dismiss","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"text":" — Clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attempts"},{"type":"text","text":". Does not modify "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".regenerateChallenge","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Replaces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge"},{"text":" with a freshly generated one. Useful for a “new question” button.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".submitAnswer(Int)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Compares against ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge.expected"},{"text":". Returns an effect that dispatches either ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerAccepted(reason:)"},{"text":" (with the current ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pendingReason"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerRejected"},{"text":". No-op if ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".answerAccepted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — Inserts ","type":"text"},{"code":"reason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into ","type":"text"},{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", clears ","type":"text"},{"code":"pendingReason","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"attempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerRejected"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — Increments "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attempts"},{"type":"text","text":" and regenerates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"challenge"},{"type":"text","text":" so the user faces a new problem."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Session-pass-behavior","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Session-pass behavior"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once a reason is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"passedReasons"},{"type":"text","text":", subsequent "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls for that same reason short-circuit: the plugin dispatches "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerAccepted(reason:)"},{"type":"text","text":" immediately without presenting a challenge. This is intentional — it lets feature reducers re-issue the gate request after re-entering a flow, while only prompting the user once per session."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"passedReasons","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set<String>"},{"type":"text","text":", so use distinct reason keys per gated action when you want them to clear independently. To force a re-challenge, mutate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.parentalGate.passedReasons"},{"text":" from your own reducer (for example, in response to an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app\/lock"},{"text":" action).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Customizing the challenge","level":2,"anchor":"Customizing-the-challenge"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalChallengeSource"},{"type":"text","text":" is a single-closure container. To plug in your own generator — different operand ranges, alternative operations, locale-specific phrasing of operands — construct one directly:"}]},{"code":["let source = ParentalChallengeSource {","    let left = Int.random(in: 50...99)","    let right = Int.random(in: 50...99)","    return MathChallenge(left: left, right: right, op: .plus)","}","","let plugin = ParentalGatePlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.parentalGate,","    action: AppAction.parentalGate,","    extractAction: { if case .parentalGate(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    challengeSource: source",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generator runs synchronously each time the plugin needs a new challenge (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".request"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".regenerateChallenge"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".answerRejected"},{"text":"). Keep it cheap and pure — no I\/O.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","type":"topic","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Macros","abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@SwiduxState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@SwiduxNested","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the two macros that generate the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","title":"Persistence Middleware","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","title":"KeyValueStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","type":"topic","title":"Add a Parental Gate","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","title":"Undo \/ Redo","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","type":"topic","title":"Plugin Architecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]}}}